    75	## Reference: what the script enforces (context, not a re-check)
    76	
    77	tests_qc.py decides these mechanically and owns the verdict on them. They are written out here so you know the shapes your own judgement calls depend on. Do not re-derive them and do not raise a finding from this section. Where the script reports a failure here, confirm it in the file and carry it into your report.
    78	
    79	- TS-S1 test_output.py exists, parses as Python, imports `criterion` and `criteria` from `rewardkit`, and no check function name is defined twice. Python silently keeps only the last definition of a duplicated name, so a duplicate means a check the author believes exists never runs. Each check is a top-level function decorated with `@criterion(description=...)` carrying a non-empty description, whose only parameter is `workspace`.
    80	- TS-S2 There are at least 10 checks; more than 35 is bloat worth a warn and a redundancy review.
    81	- TS-S3 Every registration is a module-level `criteria.<name>(weight=W)` call with W an integer literal from {5, 3, 1, -1, -3, -5}. Zero, two, floats, strings, a missing weight and any extra argument are all violations. A `tests/test_weights.json` file is forbidden outright.
