    33	- AL-2 Everything promised is graded. Enumerate from `instruction.md` alone. The unit here is what the PROMPT promises, not everything any shipped file happens to say, so a spec that documents more than this task asks for does not turn its spare detail into ungraded promises. Where the prompt delegates instead of restating ("your output must conform to `schema.json`"), follow the pointer and enumerate the delegated rules the delegation actually invokes, not the whole file: otherwise one sentence collapses a forty-field schema into a single row, and one test touching one field looks like full coverage. For each requirement so enumerated, point to the test or the judged criterion that checks it; either channel satisfies this. An ungraded promise invites solutions that skip it. Strict fail; name the requirement and state that no test or criterion covers it.
