    66	- AL-20 No network exfiltration or supply-chain risk: no curl/wget piped to a shell, no downloading and executing code from URLs, nothing that transmits bundle contents or grading data outward. The task runs offline, so there must be no outbound calls at all in the instruction, the Dockerfile's runtime path, the solution or the tests; AL-15 owns the plain "this cannot work offline" case, while what stays a fail here, and would stay one under any policy, is malicious use: exfiltration of secrets, bundle contents or grading data, and downloading then executing code. Fail. One exception: the official uv installer piped to a shell at build time in `environment/Dockerfile`, exactly `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh`, as in the recommended DS-29 block. Any other piped download, or this one anywhere else (tests/Dockerfile, solve.sh, test.sh, the checks), still fails.
