Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/03_Tests_QC.md:46:- TS-15 Negative checks use inverted polarity: the check returns True when the cheat is present, so an honest agent makes it return False and escapes the penalty; the negative weight does the punishing. Verify each negative check actually implements this direction; a check that returns True for honest work punishes honest agents. Each negative check should carry an inline comment stating the inversion.
