master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:1:# QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK v3 (how to clear a QC finding without softening a lever)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:3:Status: v3 ACTIVE 27 Oct 2026 18:45 (Ayush decisions 2, 3, "proceed"; pipeline v4 PLAN `master_chat_work/_dev_research/pipeline_v4/PLAN.md`): row NEW-CHECK no longer asks for count <= 35 (TS-23 option A, matches row TS-23); new section 1b guard rules G1-G7 (QC loop study 3b00450: 67 of 255 later findings were caused by fixes, at least 22 directed by the fix prompt, mostly pasted QC "Fix:" text). Supersedes v2. v2 history: v2 ACTIVE 24 Oct 2026 (plan v1 Part 1, from qc_reverse A checks.json and B FIX_SIDE_EFFECTS / DEFENCES / VARIANCE: IN-15 scope, [24 Oct 12:50: caps removed, genuine-minimum warns, see CHANGELOG], rows JD-5, NEW-CHECK, NOISE, defence rule; reflex gate removed from section 3). v1 was ACTIVE 23 Oct 2026 11:05 IST (Ayush: "we have to bypass the QC so that we can maintain the levers, traps etc ... a regular fix can make it soft and easy"). Live kit at writing: 71a653b2. Read with `LEVER_RULES_v1.md` (W/G/J rules) and `QC_RULINGS.md` (precedents). A change is a new file `QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md` plus a CHANGELOG line.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:5:In place 25 Oct (QC push 5574d77e, review ae47772, Ayush decision 1): rule-of-engagement scope narrowed (04:95, 05:21); direction (4b) ship one determinate fact; IN-15 and SUGGEST re-quote 01:45; new rows IN-17 and AL-1; AL-2 enumerated from the prompt (05:33); AL-27 widened to established orderings (05:38); CL-4 exemption first for whole-document tests (LEVER_RULES_v2 G1).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:7:Used by: the master when writing P12 `[[FIX_DIRECTIONS]]` (every line cites a row id below); P12 sessions (Phase 1 step 6, Phase 2 trap-survival); P2 / P4 / P9 sessions when writing `WORK/QC_DEFENCE.md` (each entry names its row and the pre-agreed fix).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:9:## 0. The idea: pass QC on merit, keep the trap at full strength
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:10:"Bypass" here means: satisfy exactly what the rule demands and nothing more. It never means hiding a defect from QC. A dodge fails twice: P11 re-runs blind, the PL re-runs, and the kit treats the dodges themselves as findings (a vague rule fails IN-15, "Vagueness counts against the author" 01:45; a wrong label fails JD-15, "report the label as the defect" 04:92).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:12:What the kit demands, and what it does NOT demand (quote these in KEEP / REBUT lines):
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:15:| every rule of engagement (scope, which files may change, tools, procedural order, negatives) stated in a file the agent can read (IN-15 01:45, AL-1 carve-out 05:21); every deliverable-property rule (formats, literals, conventions, output precedence) stated OR settled by one determinate fact in the copied input, a shipped example included (AL-1 05:21-32, FC:492, 04:95) | the rule in the instruction or beside its use, or a pointer to its file: "you must not ask for the rules to be copied into the prompt", "need not name the file" (01:45); a sentence for a fact the input determines (05:21) |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:16:| one reading for anything graded, shown by all three parts (IN-16) | polished or explicit prose: "Wording you merely find loose, terse or unpolished is not this check"; "If both readings would satisfy every test and every criterion, there is no defect" (01:46) |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:17:| every promise of instruction.md (plus each delegated rule it invokes, 05:33) graded by an input that triggers it, including orderings the input establishes (AL-2, AL-27 05:38) | fewer rules or simpler data |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:18:| the oracle satisfies every criterion (JD-7) | weaker criteria |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:19:| one observable paid once (TS-26, JD-14); one act <= -5 (AL-28, negatives only) | fewer cascading whole-document tests (G1, accepted district-heat v3:185) |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:20:| no answer recoverable from the data (DS-4); no instruction sentence announcing what the input establishes (IN-17 01:47) | explanations, worked examples, hints, rule counts |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:21:| at least 10 checks and 8 criteria, no upper cap (Ayush 24 Oct 12:50); the kit WARN above 35 checks (TS-23, 03:62) is recorded with the count | merging or dropping any check to reach a count |
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:23:Fix directions that keep the trap (prefer in this order): (1) fix the oracle or TRUTH.md; (2) add hidden triggering inputs; (3) narrow, re-label or re-scope a criterion or a negative; (4) merge low-value format or presence checks; (4b) for an AL-1 / TS-19 / IN-16 finding on a deliverable property: ship one determinate fact that contradicts the wrong reading (a config value, a separating record, a listed set) and add its EVIDENCE_MAP row, never a solved list or answer (W11); (5) state a missing rule once, neutrally, in the file that governs that data.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:24:Soft directions (never, unless Ayush says so for one finding): delete a rule, move a rule next to its use or into instruction.md, add an example where the readings differ, explain why a reading is wrong, say how many rules there are, loosen a criterion to fit the oracle, drop or merge a check that a lever's wrong reading fails, shrink or simplify hidden data, put the separating row in shipped data (W5 allows L5 only).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_FIX_PLAYBOOK_v3.md:29:| IN-15 | graded rule stated nowhere | State it once as a bare property in the file that governs that data, in that file's own vocabulary (W2, W3); no example, no "note", no new pointer in the instruction beyond the existing "rules are in X". If a negative's trigger list is wider than its sentence, narrow the test to the sentence. | Sentence in instruction.md beside the step; bold / "important"; an example that separates the readings; naming the trap; widening the sentence to fit the test. | dispatch v2:40 (negative narrowed); kit 01:45 "any file inside the input directories ... need not name the file" |
