master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:142:- Q1 JD-7 trajectory criteria: "you may judge in traj but it should be reflected in oracle as well, so phrase your rubric so it passes oracle." -> Probe criteria allowed; solve.sh must perform and print each probe act (JD-7 kept, CONFLICTS C1 path).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:143:- Q2 JD-15 probe wording ("The agent runs its program on one input where <stated branch> applies and shows that record and the program's decision", w3): "yes, pass." -> odds-raising, passes. Closes the open J2 note in Patterns below.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:144:- Q3 CL-4 stated all-corpora gate: "search for related checks in qc and if they pass it passes. the concept is to not test on hidden keys, if you want to test then at least mention the keys in contract somewhere, no or minimal explanation is fine." -> One stated gate allowed when the related checks pass; every key/field/value form a test reads must be named somewhere in the shipped contract (explanation may be minimal).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:145:- Q4 IN-17 naming what changes on fresh inputs: "depends on you if you can bring pass rate down even when mentioning those things fine by me, but i wouldn't recommend mentioning anything more than necessary." -> Allowed, not recommended; default is no rerun-axis sentence, mention only what is necessary.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:147:- Q5 (26 Oct 18:55, Ayush relayed): "is a task deliverable if Opus passes 100% of tests but the final score is below 70 because of the rubric? Example: tariff, tests 100, rubric 18, final 59." Sugam: "no". -> gate = tests < 100 AND final < 70; judge-only rebuilds cannot rescue tests-100 tasks.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:149:## Carry-over between QC rounds (Ayush decision 2, 27 Oct; QC loop study 3b00450)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:150:Round 2 and later run in recheck mode (P11 v3 MODE recheck). The reviewer receives the previous report, the task's `KEPT.md` (each kept item with its kit-line reason) and `CHANGED_LINES` (`diff -U0` between the previous and current QC copies). A finding on an unchanged line, or on a kept item, must answer the earlier PASS or KEEP reason with a kit line; otherwise it is recorded as "acknowledged" (not a fail) and the master adds a FP_DOSSIER row. Kit scripts still run in full every round. Evidence: findings per round fell 126, 48, 53, 44, 38, 44, 20, 7, 1; 50 of 255 later findings re-flagged kept items, 67 were caused by fixes.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:153:- QC accepts a natural cascade: one whole-document test per view per hidden extract (district-heat v3:185, cohort v2:183). G1 is QC-safe as built.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:154:- TS-26 and AL-28 failures in our history were all on negatives, never on positive cascades (vendor v1:53, v3:34, v1:54, dispatch v2:42). Group negatives by act and make overlapping ones stand down (vendor v4:451).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:155:- A judge negative that shadows a test negative is stacking across layers (vendor v1:54, dispatch v2:42); give each act one layer only.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:159:- Code-quality and figure criteria failed JD-7 against our own oracle 4 times (district-heat v1:363, vendor v2:47, cohort v1:41, dispatch v2:41): run the oracle against every criterion before QC.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:160:- Fixes created new findings: the TS-13 split created a TS-25 absence check (schema v3:353), a cast fix folded a second rule into a check (schema v4:30). P12 v2 must re-check the rules its fix touches.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/QC_RULINGS.md:162:- No QC ruling yet exists on J2 conduct criteria ("constructs its own input ... and checks ..."); the pilots are the first test (PL Q46 open).

