master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:61:## 5. Lever candidates
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:64:| LC1 | Bounded induction: a withheld fact with a stated finite domain. The shipped instance is degenerate (many fits work); each hidden instance admits one fit, under the exact rule only | 59417607 (TRUTH.md:29,69), 18b5d99f, 6d12f970 | Legal under Never 6 if the domain is stated and the deciding fact is in EVIDENCE_MAP. Never 11: at most one unlabelled witness, no shipped rollups or expected totals | Build: state the domain in the data dictionary; generate hidden instances with coupled groups larger than shipped | Uniqueness script per hidden instance; 3 blind programs lose >= 25% of test points by valid-but-wrong output |
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:65:| LC2 | G3a weight asymmetry: shipped exact checks w1, hidden-instance checks w5 | 59417607 7.22, 18b5d99f 7.77, d49e259f 6.38 | Legal (G3 hidden share); an amplifier, not a lever | Harden: reweight existing checks; keep shipped checks as cheap sanity | stacking_check: a first-write program passes shipped and stays <= 75 on tests |
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:66:| LC3 | J11 counterfactual figures: the judge asks for exact what-if figures that need the delivered program re-run on a changed input | 59417607 7/8 wrong, aa314fee 8/8, 5b2b0901; LEAK_LIBRARY:12 says headline figures leak | Legal (J1: not computable by the same code path on shipped data); the questions must be stated in the instruction | 4-8 what-ifs, each flipping one stated parameter that propagates through carried state | Oracle computes each figure by a program rerun; blind run misses >= 3 |
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:67:| LC4 | Interlocking allocation plus never-healing carried state: each grant depends on every claim in its cell, and an early error persists to the end | aa314fee (TRUTH.md:7-8), b5c7b14c reserve | Legal (stated rules; L3/P-2) | One shared level per cell; a carried lot with survival; whole-ledger exact checks | A one-rule-flip program loses >= 25% while invariants still pass |
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:68:| LC5 | Per-field-class authority order: a different precedence per field class, authority over recency | df8f123b (TRUTH.md:15-25) | Legal if each class's order is written once, without naming the uniform misreading (Never 8) | Spread the 3 class tables over 2-3 documents (L4) | A uniform-order program loses >= 25%, shipped-only tests suffice |
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:69:| LC6 | T1 hazard-slice tests: one hidden check per data hazard. Partial credit tracks the hazards covered | 80202e15, 9f5486ac | Legal; avoid a global HELD gate that zeroes everything (P14: PARTLY) | Harden: split whole-document checks by hazard family (TS-13 one property per check) | The per-hazard pass pattern of blind runs differs from the oracle's on >= 4 slices |
master_chat_work/20261028_upgrade/R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:71:Not levers for us (holes): unbounded induction, where forms or meanings are unstated (8defd7be, d49e259f, 5b2b0901; breaks Never 6, and ships reference outputs, breaking Never 11); instructed effort caps (5b2b0901); judge-only bands with P <= 20 (725e575c).
