master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:86:New builds are siblings of P-1 to P-3 shapes. Stated-rule levers (L1-L11, S1, S3, S5, S6, H1-H9, T1-T4) are PAUSED, not discarded: no new hardening round relies on them until the lever audit (`prompts/drafts/lever_audit/PLAN.md`) checks each against delivered trajectories. A lever the audit finds not helpful is marked DISABLED here with its evidence; nothing is deleted.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:87:- [v3.4: Ayush decision 4, 27 Oct] Law-1 filter. A test lever counts only when the strongest plausible solvers (the probe agent's program, every blind program, every generic solver in the kill test) lose by a valid but wrong document. Loss by timeout or crash does not count: a timeout tells the agent to fix its program and it recovers. Every kill table splits each solver's loss into WRONG / TIMEOUT / CRASH. P-1 and P-3 pass only with a WRONG stage (for example a plausible faster method that returns a feasible but non-optimal or wrongly carried figure). P-2 counts only with a stage where a plausible program passes the shipped history and is wrong on the hidden one (pass rate below 1 for plausible programs), not just slow.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:88:- [v3.5: Ayush answer B, 27 Oct 20:10] Law-1 amended. A TIMEOUT or CRASH loss also counts ("hidden-scale loss") when all three hold: (1) no shipped input (shipped data, visible tests, any example in the docs) makes the plausible program time out or crash, so the agent sees no warning; (2) the limit it hits is stated: a runtime sentence in the docs (no method words), or the task's declared container memory for a crash; (3) the measured cost on plausible programs is 10-30% of positive test points and stays inside the lever checks: each lever corpus runs in its own call, so a timeout never costs non-lever checks. Evidence: sentinel harness attempts 5-7, real Opus lost 28 test points by timeout on hidden sizes and did not recover. A lever that fails (1)-(3) still needs a WRONG stage. Kill tables keep the WRONG / TIMEOUT / CRASH split and add a column 'shipped inputs fast: yes/no'.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:89:- [v3.6: Ayush 27 Oct 22:30, new gate tests < 85, rubric < 85, final < 50; SUPERSEDED by the v3.7 bullet below] Overrides every 10-30% lever-cost figure (v3.5 condition 3, section 6, templates): a test lever now costs 25-40% of positive test points, and a plain first-write program and the all-but-one program aim at tests <= 75. Blind bar: each of the 3 fresh blind reads scores tests <= 80, its losses WRONG output or v3.5 hidden-scale loss. Judge: probe band with predicted probe mid 15-20. Overnight auto runs: the master may send "go" at DESIGN READY when the kill table passes (every generic solver and every blind program loses >= 15% of lever points, shipped inputs fast, reference <= 1/4 of the stated limit); otherwise Needs Ayush.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:90:- [v3.7: Ayush 28 Oct "Target <40 now"; upgrade plan v2 C2, 29 Oct] Replaces the v3.6 bullet above. Plain first-write and all-but-one programs aim at tests <= 60. Blind bar: each of the 3 fresh blind reads scores tests <= 65 (none above 70), its losses WRONG output or v3.5 hidden-scale loss. Judge: probe band, predicted probe mid <= 20. DESIGN READY needs, in DESIGN.md: (a) predicted final = (predicted first-write tests + predicted judge mid)/2 <= 35 (5 points margin for the final spread; same-bytes spread, section 6 v3.4 bullet); (b) lever share >= 40% of positive test weight (if the lever is fully lost and all else passes, tests <= 60), with the held-out w5 tier >= 50% when the N2 shape is used; (c) blind ceiling: no blind program above tests 65; (d) verifier worst case <= 90% of the stated verifier limit; (e) the kill table rule (every generic solver and every blind program loses >= 15% of lever points by WRONG output, or v3.5 hidden-scale loss; shipped inputs fast; reference <= 1/4 of the stated limit) unchanged. Overnight go at DESIGN READY unchanged. Evidence: final < 40 needs tests + rubric < 80; our 10 valid gate runs mean tests 78.7, rubric 23.5, 1 below 40 (upgrade R3 FINDINGS:137).
