master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:121:### 1b. Opus-habit bank (default lever picks; 24 Oct second read of the 6 delivered tasks)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:124:- H2 float rounding: binary float or half-up where the rule says exact decimal, half-even, at a stated step, with at least 3 planted ties (L8; pa M2).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:130:- [v3: g1/C_18b5d99f.md:32, g1/C_3f39299a.md:45-46] H8 first fit: returns the first candidate that fits instead of checking that exactly one fits (S3).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:131:- [v3: g1 GS:5-10, g3/C_0b27b9dc.md:65] H9 shipped-only self-test: checks aggregates and invariants on shipped data, never builds an input that fires a stated branch (S2, S8, and the probe band).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:134:Habit levers leak by writing, not by data (metered probe 1: tests 199/199 with H1-H4 all held). Opus builds its own generator and tie fixture for every explicit sentence. A habit lever trips only when written like this:
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:138:- H4: only when the normalisation lives in one file's reading convention (slo); otherwise noise.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:140:- Opus's method (sentinel probe 1): it reads every rule file in one loop and transliterates each sentence using the per-line field the sentence names. Key the rule from a different file than the field it reads, and make the shipped control reconcile under both readings.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:144:## 2. Writing rules. Every rule of engagement stated (IN-15); every graded rule has one reading (IN-16), from a sentence or from determinate evidence (0b).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:148:- W4. An override names the field exactly.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:154:- W10. [v3: CONFLICTS C10 and breadth, g2 GS:23, g3 GS:27] One rule register. `docs/` (or the task's equivalent) holds a register file naming every governing file; each rule is one sentence in the file that governs its data (W2). instruction.md states the job, the output paths, whole-document exactness, the rerun promise (G5) and the rules of engagement (work directory, process order, files that may change, exact invocation). It states no rule of the computation. Wholesale delegation ("follow the register") makes every rule it invokes an AL-2 row (05:33).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:158:## 3. Grading rules
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:159:Kit limits: TS-26 forbids two tests reading the same observable with the same logic; TS-13 one property per test; AL-28 applies to negatives only, one act costs at most -5 across both layers. CL-4 (FC:491) is exempted by "an instruction that states out loud that only an exact match counts".
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:160:- G1. Whole-document exact grading per hidden corpus. Tests compare each output document whole, exactly, on each hidden corpus, provided instruction.md states that only an exact match counts (G5); quote FC:491 in QC_DEFENCE under CL-4. Report the one-fact-wrong score anyway. Every amplified slip must trace to a stated single-reading rule or an L11 rule (a GENUINE loss), never to an ambiguity, an unstated rule or an oracle defect (G9). A COUPLING quantity still multiplies a slip legitimately. [v3: CONFLICTS C3; g2/C_37a0c3d6.md:48 QC passed a stated 9-corpus gate; g1 GS:46-52 b42c61b9 WARN] At most one stated cross-corpus gate per task ("a family counts only when every one of its corpora is exact"), with its sentence in instruction.md; the related QC checks (CL-4, TS-19, AL-28) must pass; and every key, field and value form any test reads must be named somewhere in the shipped contract (minimal explanation is fine). Never grade a key the agent cannot read. [QL 26 Oct, Q3: "search for related checks in qc and if they pass it passes. the concept is to not test on hidden keys, if you want to test then at least mention the keys in contract somewhere, no or minimal explanation is fine."]
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:161:- G1a. [v3: g2/C_3def42a3.md:62-64] Per-row ownership (the safe alternative to a gate). Each output row or byte is owned by exactly one test (`OWNED` map); shared columns are masked in every test except their owner. One slip then costs its rows in one test, and a test that compared nothing never passes (`_tier_ok`, g2/C_3def42a3.md:67).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:163:- G3. [v3: CONFLICTS C2, g1 GS:23, g2 GS:47-58] Hidden share follows the shape. Shape D: at least 70% of positive weight on generated hidden corpora. Shape B: no floor; shipped whole-family exact may carry the weight. Every shape: at least one hidden rerun per output family. Shares are measured by following the call graph (section 5), never by test names.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:165:- G5. The instruction states whole-document exactness, e.g. "each output document is graded whole on fresh inputs, and only an exact match counts" (FC:491, TS-19), without naming any lever. [v3: CONFLICTS C13; 18b5d99f instruction.md:7, 37a0c3d6 instruction.md:3] It also states the rerun promise: the program is run again on fresh inputs of the same layout. Naming which axes change (sizes, ids, dates, which stated branches occur) is allowed by QC but off by default: instruction.md mentions only what is necessary, with no axis list [QL 26 Oct, Q4: "depends on you if you can bring pass rate down even when mentioning those things fine by me, but i wouldn't recommend mentioning anything more than necessary."]. It never names a branch as tricky. Do NOT add "at other scales" or "other sizes" wording. No self-check paragraph ("recompute a second way", "outside the program", "on a copy you changed").
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:166:- G6. At least 2 mutation tests. Stock recipes: shuffle rows + scale one rate curve by a non-round factor; relocate or rename the corpus directory; rotate row order; delete one declared source (expect a non-zero exit naming it); run as non-root from a foreign cwd; run twice and compare. [v3: CONFLICTS C15, 0b27b9dc test_output.py:4386-4457, g3 GS:21] A mutation or variant test counts only on corpora where the plain hidden run of the same family is exact, so one slip is not charged twice.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:169:- G8a. [v3: g4/C_8d3e20fb.md:11, :40; test_output.py:513-533; g4 GS:116-122] Stated invocation. instruction.md states the exact command (interpreter, flags, cwd, arguments) the tests use to run the program; the tests run exactly that. No unstated `python -I`, no unstated cwd.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:170:- G9. Expected values are independent of the oracle: `check_exact.py` recomputes from the visible documents only. For every footnote, erratum or correction mechanism, an override-removal probe proves the oracle reads it. [v3: 7c2e77a1 46 test pts, g1 GS:72-77] Never hard-code shipped expected values from the oracle alone; a second reference must agree.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:177:## 4. Judge rules
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:180:- J2. [v3: CONFLICTS C1; g3 GS:25, g3/C_0b27b9dc.md:38, :66] Probe band. 8 to 16 probe criteria, each w3, importance "important", type "process", evaluation_target "trajectory", together 55-70% of positive judge weight. Each names ONE act Opus skips and the requirement it serves (04:92 "name the requirement the conduct SERVES"). Pick from the probe templates P-a to P-h below. The oracle shows every probe act (JD-7 04:76): solve.sh's self-check stage performs each probe act and prints `check <id> ok` plus the one witness line (the input id and the decision). [QL 26 Oct, Q1: "you may judge in traj but it should be reflected in oracle as well, so phrase your rubric so it passes oracle." A trajectory criterion is allowed only when the oracle shows it.] The agent never sees the oracle trajectory, so this costs no hardness. Never echo probe wording in instruction.md.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:183:  - P-b one-instance witness: "The agent shows at least one <item id> where <stated condition> holds together with the decision its program made for it." (serves: <family> exactness)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:185:  - P-d altered-copy rerun: "The agent runs <program> on a copy of the inputs in which it changed <a value the rule reads>, and shows that <dependent output> changed." (not an exact copy: 56fe3bdd R7 failed on an exact copy, g3/C_56fe3bdd.md:55)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:208:- J9. [v3: folded into J2a P-d] The altered-copy rerun is probe P-d.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:210:- Band arithmetic (design target; Opus pass rates from peers: probes 3 of 16 and 4 of 18, g3/C_0b27b9dc.md:65, g3/C_7e0d8feb.md:41; J6 and J4-passes vary): 12 probes x3 = 36, J4 3, J6 3, J10 order 3 = 45 positive. Expected Opus: probes 25% = 9, J6 3, J4 0-3, J10 1.5 = 13.5-16.5 of 45 = 30-37%, minus any fired honesty negative.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:211:- `WORK/JUDGE_MAP.md`: one row per criterion `| id | requirement it serves (sentence file:line) | oracle shows it at (solve.sh line / printed check) | test it must not overlap |`. A criterion with no oracle-shows entry is removed (JD-7). Never add keys to `[criterion.annotations]` (judge_qc J6 allows exactly mode, type, evaluation_target, importance).
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:212:- Kit standing of each part: probes w3 = odds-raising, pass under JD-15 Step 2 (04:92 "an odds-raising approach weighted 1 or 3 passes"); oracle shows them (JD-7 kept); trajectory observable differs from every test (JD-8 04:77, 04:81 "artifact vs trajectory"); J10 quotes a sentence (JD-16 04:93-97); J4 lists only JD-18 items (04:99). The probe wording ("shows one instance", "runs on an input where <stated branch> applies") passes as odds-raising per QL 26 Oct, Q2: "yes, pass." (QC_RULINGS.md section "QL answers 26 Oct 2026").
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:214:## 5. STACKING_CHECK gate (every build, harden and fix round, before P11)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:223:- (h) [v3] JUDGE_MAP: probe count 8-16, probe share 55-70% of positive judge weight, every criterion with an oracle-shows entry.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:227:## 6. Probe gate and evidence rules (Ayush decisions 7, 8, 11; kill rule 26 Oct)
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:229:- Blind read before every probe: 3 fresh P13 blind-solve sessions (each sees only a copy of instruction.md and environment/). Score each program with the real tests and `tools/loss.py`. A rule or lever counts only when at least 2 of the 3 programs get it wrong.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:231:  - judge lower bound = (points of PASS criteria, probes counted PASS only when the blind CHECKS log shows the exact act) minus (fired negatives) over positive points;
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:232:  - judge upper bound = (PASS + UNSURE + every probe not contradicted by the log) over positive points; negatives counted only when shown;
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:233:  - judge mid = outcome criteria as marked, probes at the peer pass rate 25% (g3/C_0b27b9dc.md:65 3 of 16; g3/C_7e0d8feb.md:41 4 of 18);
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:235:  Before a probe: when the lower-bound final is above 70 on 2 of 3 blind reads, harden or redesign before the probe (never park; v3.2 below); queue the probe otherwise.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:236:- Harden decisions rest on 1 real harness run plus that round's blind reads. [v3: CONFLICTS C16, Ayush D2 26 Oct] The final gate: tests < 100 AND final < 70. [v3.6: Ayush 27 Oct 22:20 "new gate is test < 85 , rubrics < 85 and overall < 50"] REPLACED: the final gate is now tests < 85 AND rubric < 85 AND final < 50 on that 1 valid run (final = (tests + rubric)/2, so final < 50 needs rubric < 100 - tests: tests 80 needs rubric < 20). [v3.7: Ayush 28 Oct "Target <40 now"] REPLACED again: the final gate is tests < 85 AND rubric < 85 AND final reward < 40 on 1 valid run of the frozen QC-passed bytes before push (v3.7, Ayush 28 Oct "Target <40 now"; was 50 under v3.6, Ayush 27 Oct 22:20; was tests < 100 AND final < 70 before). Final = (tests + rubric)/2, so final < 40 needs rubric < 80 - tests; design for tests <= 60 and rubric <= 20. Tasks that met the old gate and miss the new one are hardened from their trajectory (KNOWLEDGE section T) with the proven levers (1C) and the QC-safe edits; judge target is a probe band with predicted mid 15-20. [v3.4: Ayush 27 Oct 17:17 "push needs only 1 run that is QC passed and under our gate score"] Push needs 1 valid harness run on the frozen QC-passed bytes (tree sha recorded at freeze) that meets the gate; any change after that run voids it. [v3.1: QL Sugam 26 Oct 18:55 answered "no" to "is a task deliverable with tests 100 and final < 70 via the rubric"; Ayush D2 reverted] A judge-only rebuild never rescues a tests-100 task; at least one positive test must be lost.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:239:- (Superseded by v3.2 for parking) Kill rule (Ayush 26 Oct): park when the probe's final reward (tests and judge combined, as the harness reports it) is above 70. Tests at 100 on 2 valid runs park the task whatever the final (QL 26 Oct 18:55); otherwise tests alone never park a task: delivered peers pass with tests 85-96 and a low judge (0b27b9dc 96.5/26, 7e0d8feb 94/33, e13fd332 90/25). [v3: CONFLICTS C9, Ayush D3 26 Oct; g2/C_daaca581_DIFF.md] Variance band: above 75, park; 65 to 75, run a second probe and park when the mean final is above 70; below 65, keep. A round marked LAST is the last.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:240:- [v3.3: Ayush 27 Oct, own iteration evidence] Measure and order. The fresh blind read (3 P13 sessions, never the old agent program or a worker reflex program) is the only measure of a round; a round counts only when fresh blind programs lose at least 10% of positive test weight. The design blind also tries the strongest generic solver for the core (bitset subset-sum, meet-in-the-middle, small-width DP, sweep); if it is exact within the time limit, redesign before the full build. One QC runs before the first probe, and every finding, minors included, is fixed in one pass.
master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:244:- A score from a run with a grader error (permission, crash, timeout, missing file) is never a baseline. Only `valid: true` lines in `registry/scores.jsonl` count.
