@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Hardness levers against the live QC kit
+
+`TB` means `/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench`; all citations below are `TB`-relative. The safe boundary is: a graded output fact must be stated or *determinate* in copied input; silence is not evidence. A graded scope/tool/order prohibition must be stated. A conduct criterion can remain unstated if every competent route meets it or the act raises the chance of a correct result. These are `01_Instruction_QC.md:38,45-47`, `05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:21-32`, and `04_Judge_QC.md:92-97`. The agent may be asked *what* to produce and where; the hidden data property, worked answer, scoring mechanism and solution recipe may be withheld (`01_Instruction_QC.md:32,39,44,47`).
+
+| Lever | QC checks touched | QC-clean build: state / withhold / prove |
+|---|---|---|
+| P-1 computational core | IN-14, DS-10/21, TS-11/19/29, AL-17, CL-10 | State the result and legal input bounds; install required tools; withhold the decomposition/algorithm. Prove a competent exact solver can finish within the agent limit, the oracle within verifier limit, and the graded answer follows from the visible contract. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:81,87-90`; `02_Data_Solution_QC.md:29,70`. |
+| P-2 stateful replay | IN-8/16, DS-21, TS-19/26, AL-27, CL-4 | State state transitions, ordering and tie rules once in a copied spec; hide long streams and their final figures. Plant each transition and conflicting pair, then mutate one rule at a time. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:50,82,172`; `05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:38`. |
+| P-3 exact optimum | IN-9/14/16, DS-21, TS-19/20, CL-4/10 | State objective, feasibility and tie-break; withhold the algorithm and optimum. Put larger but in-bounds instances in the hidden tier; independently prove optimum and report one-fact score. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:83,160,170`; `Final_checklist.md:491,498`. |
+| P-4 robustness | IN-8/16, TS-16/19/29, AL-27 | State what must happen on invalid or interrupted input; hide the particular failure fixture. Keep failure checks separate, and ensure hostile output returns a check result rather than aborting rewardkit. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:84`; `03_Tests_QC.md:47,55`. |
+| P-5 / probe-band judge | JD-5/7/8/9/15/18, AL-1/28 | Judge one visible trajectory act per criterion, serving a real requirement. Its approach must be competent or odds-raising, at weight 1 or 3. Make oracle `solve.sh` demonstrate it; do not echo the probe wording in instruction. Keep test observables distinct and penalties unstacked. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:180,210-212`; `04_Judge_QC.md:92,99`. |
+| N1 pairing test and judge channels | TS-10/20, JD-8/14, AL-F0d/28 | Split by observable: tests assess artifact behaviour, judge assesses distinct process acts. Compute each 0.5 channel correctly; one action must not pay or lose twice. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:101-104`; `03_Tests_QC.md:37`; `05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:39`. |
+| N2 / LC2 held-out w5 tier | IN-8, TS-19/20/26, AL-1/27, CL-4/5 | State general rules, allowed value domains, invocation and output format. Hide seed values and answers, not a new field/key or rule. Give core hidden outcomes weight 5 and shipped sanity checks weight 1 only when importance supports it; distinguish observables and report one-fact loss. `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:90,102-104,160`; `03_Tests_QC.md:49-53`. |
+| LC1 bounded induction / L11 | IN-16/17, DS-21/25, AL-1/27, CL-5/10 | State a finite candidate domain. Withhold which candidate wins; ship an unlabelled witness that selects exactly one reading, and prove uniqueness for every hidden corpus. A sample where multiple readings fit is silence and fails. `R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:64,79`; `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:29-36,58`. |
+| LC3 counterfactual figures | IN-8/9/17, JD-7/8/15, AL-1, CL-10 | State each what-if question and perturbation in the contract; hide computed figures. Compute oracle figures independently and judge a distinct final-answer fact only if deterministic tests do not grade it. `R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:66`; `04_Judge_QC.md:76-77,92`. |
+| LC4 interlocking state | IN-8/16, TS-19/26, AL-27, CL-4 | State shared allocation and carried-shortfall rules; hide stream contents and totals. Each earlier decision should change later graded output; avoid charging one scalar in several tests. `R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:67`; `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:50,110`. |
+| LC5 per-field authority | IN-16/17, DS-3/21, AL-1/27, CL-6 | State each field class's authority order in copied documents, with a real signpost when a shipped value is stale. Do not announce which rows trigger the exception. Plant conflicting values per class and trace the winning row. `R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:68`; `Final_checklist.md:493`. |
+| LC6 hazard-slice tests | TS-13/19/20/26, AL-27, CL-4 | One check per hazard and observable, with a triggering hidden fixture. Give partial credit per repaired hazard; avoid a global gate that zeros unrelated work. `R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:69`; `03_Tests_QC.md:44,53`. |
+
+## Additional source levers in the prior studies
+
+`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:46-58,65-77` lists these building blocks. `S4_task_study/FINDINGS.md:17-30,48-52` associates held-out exact outputs, whole-output exactness and trajectory criteria with recorded loss; association is not a fairness proof. `R3_hardness_md/FINDINGS.md:95-110` calls held-out instances and process criteria proven in its sample, with weight concentration only a structural amplifier.
+
+| Source lever | QC surface and clean boundary |
+|---|---|
+| L1 green control; L2 make-it-match repair | DS-3/4/21, IN-16/17, CL-6: describe the control truthfully as a control; state the governing rule in its copied spec. A control that reconciles under two readings cannot choose between them. The decoy must be signposted as suspect when it conflicts with grading (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:48-49`; `Final_checklist.md:493`). |
+| L3 stateful stream; L4 multi-document composition | IN-8/16, AL-1/27, CL-10: state transitions and each source's authority; withhold the joined result and which branch a row takes. Mutate one rule to prove trigger depth (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:50-51`; `05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:38`). |
+| L5 strict type beside normalisation; L6 scoped definition | IN-8/16/17, TS-19, AL-1/27: state the type and scope; hide particular malformed rows and rare joins. A shipped example must actually separate readings if used as evidence (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:52-53`; `05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:26-32`). |
+| L7 rounding/unit; L8 exact-decimal recurrence; L9 factor denominator | IN-16, TS-17/18/19, CL-5/10: state precision, rounding step, units and denominator; hide final figures and tie locations. Plant ties and one-rule mutants (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:54-56`; `03_Tests_QC.md:48-50`). |
+| L10 rare joined field | IN-8/17, AL-27: state the general normalisation rule, hide the row where it matters, and plant a graded join that changes under a wrong reader (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:57`; `05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:38`). |
+| S1 breadth; S2 degenerate shipped instance; S3 unique fit | IN-8/16, TS-19/23, AL-27, CL-10: keep every rule and candidate space reachable; hidden data may fire branches absent from shipped data only when the branch rule is stated. More than 35 tests is a warn, not permission to merge distinct checks (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:67-69,175`; `03_Tests_QC.md:62`). |
+| S4 authority chain; S5 partial-authority decoy; S6 buried hidden fixture | IN-16/17, DS-3/21, AL-27, CL-6: write authority and demotion rules once, identify a superseded source in its header, and trigger each rule in hidden data. Withhold which particular file/row wins (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:70-72`). |
+| S7 digest cascade; S8 rare branch; S9 self-referential artifact; S10 provenance gate; S11 scoped exception | TS-13/19/26, AL-27, CL-4/5: state digest/branch/provenance/scope rules, hide answer values, grade distinct observable families, and measure one-fact loss. A same-fact digest cascade needs an explicit exact-match contract and still faces duplicate-payment review (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:73-77,159-172`; `Final_checklist.md:491`). |
+| Hidden scale / timeout share | DS-10/21, TS-11/29, AL-17, CL-10: state input bounds and time budget, make shipped inputs fast, keep the oracle below verifier budget, and classify wrong output separately from timeout/crash. Timing may be evidence of difficulty only when the task remains solvable and verifier errors cannot impersonate low scores (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:87-90`; `S4_task_study/FINDINGS.md:26,30`). |
+
+## Observed QC examples and limits
+
+- **Passed gate example, held-out exact and stated contract:** district-heat v11 reports overall PASS with 0 new findings (`QC/reports/district-heat-flex-procurement/v11.md:3-18`); its review traces a graded tie-break to `schema.md` and records IN-17 as clean (`v11.md:92-103`). CL-4 reports a one-fact score of 258/261 (`v11.md:42`). Its Step 10 note says only x3 oracle runs were done although the kit asks x5 (`v11.md:44`), so this is evidence for its reviewed lever and gate verdict, not a claim of kit-complete shipment.
+- **Passed gate example, action proof:** sentinel v9's Gate 05 says PASS (`QC/reports/sentinel-policy-recompute/v9.md:261`); CL-1 compares a produced config against a real delivered-tool rebuild rather than trusting the agent's report (`v9.md:271`). Its IN-17 review leaves discoveries to the agent (`v9.md:153-154`). Same x3 limitation appears at `v9.md:9-10`.
+- **Teammate examples:** `R4_teammate_repo/FINDINGS.md:23-36,61-70` identifies `42e79476` hidden exact optimization, `18b5d99f` unique fit with a stated domain, and `aa314fee` interlocking carried shortfall. Their recorded low scores are task evidence, not our QC verdicts; use their technique only after the live-kit trace above.
+- **Regression examples:** cohort v5 still found AL-27 mutants that scored 1.000 after fixtures were added (`QC/reports/cohort-retention-reconciliation/v5.md:35`); schema v14 made timeout outcome depend on scheduling (`S4_task_study/FIX_MAP.csv`, row `schema-migration-plan-repair`). These show why a fix must rerun the touched checks and one-rule mutants.
